*> Per-chunk hash dump of the standard pipeline on the real data (on demand: skipped as a pass unless CC_HASH_DUMP is set, and without the generated packs; docs/design/world-types.md structures part 8, debug against release
*> identity): on the generated vanilla-data (CC_GENERATED_DIR, read only) a standard world of seed CC_HASH_SEED (default 12345) is opened, 300 x 300 chunks around the origin are scanned
*> for the first start of every structure named in CC_HASH_KEYS (blank separated, default every structure), and the 3 x 3 chunks around each first start and 6 x 6 chunks around the
*> origin and the starts of CC_HASH_AREAS (CC_HASH_AREA_N chunks on a side, default 6; a key list of `none` scans nothing; default the origin, a snowy village, a plains village and a savanna village of seed 12345) are generated by the atomic path (GEN-JOB-RUN-ALL).
*> Every chunk prints `HASH <what> <cx> <cz> <marker y> <crc32>` (the chunk bytes), and `TIME <what> <cx> <cz> <ms>` (not part of an identity check): run it from a debug build and from a
*> release build and diff the HASH lines and the ENT lines (`ENT <what> <cx> <cz> <entity requests> <structure boxes> <crc32>`: the entity channel's digest, GENENT.cpy). The driver asserts only that it ran (the hashes have no expected value of their own: that is the comparison between the two builds).
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-GEN-HASHES.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY COREAPI.
 COPY STRUCTDATA.
 COPY CELLS.
 COPY GENENT.
 01 WS-DIR                 PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-ENV                 PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-KEYS                PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-AREAS               PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-FILE                PIC X(1100).
 01 WS-FILE-INFO           PIC X(16).
 01 WS-DIM                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-KEY                 PIC X(80).
 01 WS-POINTER             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LEN                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SX                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SZ                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-J                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-K                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-FOUND-N             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-WANT-N              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-WANT.
    05 WS-W OCCURS 40 TIMES.
       10 WW-KEY           PIC X(80).
       10 WW-ROW           BINARY-LONG.
       10 WW-FOUND         BINARY-LONG.
       10 WW-CX            BINARY-LONG.
       10 WW-CZ            BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ALL                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-REF                 PIC X(304640).
 01 WS-REF-Y               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CRC                 BINARY-LONG UNSIGNED.
 01 WS-CRC-LEN             BINARY-LONG VALUE 304640.
 01 WS-CLOCK               PIC X(21).
 01 WS-T0                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-T1                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-MS                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-E1                  PIC -(7)9.
 01 WS-E2                  PIC -(7)9.
 01 WS-E3                  PIC -(7)9.
 01 WS-E4                  PIC Z(9)9.
 01 WS-E5                  PIC Z(7)9.
 01 WS-CX                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CZ                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-X0                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-Z0                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-N                   BINARY-LONG.
*> the entity digest: a CRC of the entity requests (each entry up to its compound's last byte) and of the structure boxes of the chunk
 01 WS-ENT-CRC             BINARY-LONG UNSIGNED.
 01 WS-ENT-LEN             BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ENT-I               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-E6                  PIC Z(9)9.
 01 WS-E7                  PIC Z(9)9.
 01 WS-WHAT                PIC X(80).
 01 WS-CHUNKS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-AREA-N              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-A1                  PIC X(12).
 01 WS-A2                  PIC X(12).
 01 WS-DEFAULT-KEYS        PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-DEFAULT-AREAS       PIC X(1024) VALUE "0,0 89,105 -134,36 -66,-98".
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-ENV
     ACCEPT WS-ENV FROM ENVIRONMENT "CC_HASH_DUMP"
     IF WS-ENV = SPACES
         MOVE "test gen hashes CC_HASH_DUMP is not set, skipped (an on-demand dump, not a gate test)" TO TL-CASE
         MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
         CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
         STOP RUN
     END-IF
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-ENV
     ACCEPT WS-ENV FROM ENVIRONMENT "CC_GENERATED_DIR"
     IF WS-ENV = SPACES
         MOVE "/tmp/cc-test/generated" TO WS-DIR
     ELSE
         MOVE WS-ENV TO WS-DIR
     END-IF
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-FILE
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-DIR TRAILING) "/vanilla-data/pack.mcmeta" X"00" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-FILE
     CALL "CBL_CHECK_FILE_EXIST" USING WS-FILE WS-FILE-INFO
     IF RETURN-CODE NOT = 0
         MOVE "test gen hashes no generated packs here, skipped" TO TL-CASE
         MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
         MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
         CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
         STOP RUN
     END-IF
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS
     MOVE 1 TO WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:village_plains " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:village_desert " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:village_snowy " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:village_savanna " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:village_taiga " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:pillager_outpost " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:mineshaft " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:mineshaft_mesa " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:igloo " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:shipwreck " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:shipwreck_beached " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:ocean_ruin_warm " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:ocean_ruin_cold " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:ruined_portal " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:ruined_portal_desert " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:ruined_portal_jungle " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:ruined_portal_swamp " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:ruined_portal_mountain " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:ruined_portal_ocean " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:swamp_hut " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:jungle_pyramid " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:desert_pyramid " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     STRING "minecraft:buried_treasure " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-DEFAULT-KEYS WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-ENV
     ACCEPT WS-ENV FROM ENVIRONMENT "CC_HASH_KEYS"
     MOVE WS-DEFAULT-KEYS TO WS-KEYS
     IF WS-ENV NOT = SPACES
         MOVE WS-ENV TO WS-KEYS
     END-IF
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-ENV
     ACCEPT WS-ENV FROM ENVIRONMENT "CC_HASH_AREAS"
     MOVE WS-DEFAULT-AREAS TO WS-AREAS
     IF WS-ENV NOT = SPACES
         MOVE WS-ENV TO WS-AREAS
     END-IF
     MOVE 6 TO WS-AREA-N
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-ENV
     ACCEPT WS-ENV FROM ENVIRONMENT "CC_HASH_AREA_N"
     IF WS-ENV NOT = SPACES
         COMPUTE WS-AREA-N = FUNCTION NUMVAL(WS-ENV)
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-SETTINGS" USING CORE-SETTINGS
     MOVE "standard" TO CS-WORLD-TYPE
     MOVE WS-DIR TO CS-GENERATED-DIR
     MOVE 2 TO CS-VIEW-DISTANCE
     MOVE "12345" TO CS-SEED-TEXT
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-ENV
     ACCEPT WS-ENV FROM ENVIRONMENT "CC_HASH_SEED"
     IF WS-ENV NOT = SPACES
         MOVE WS-ENV(1:32) TO CS-SEED-TEXT
     END-IF
     CALL "TEST-OPEN-WORLD" USING CORE-SETTINGS
     MOVE CW-DIM(1) TO WS-DIM
*>   the wanted structures
     MOVE 0 TO WS-WANT-N WS-FOUND-N
     MOVE 1 TO WS-POINTER
     PERFORM UNTIL WS-POINTER > 1024 OR WS-WANT-N >= 40
         MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
         UNSTRING WS-KEYS DELIMITED BY ALL SPACES INTO WS-KEY WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
         IF WS-KEY = SPACES
             EXIT PERFORM
         END-IF
         ADD 1 TO WS-WANT-N
         MOVE WS-KEY TO WW-KEY(WS-WANT-N)
         MOVE 0 TO WW-ROW(WS-WANT-N) WW-FOUND(WS-WANT-N)
         PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > SD-ST-COUNT
             IF SDT-KEY(WS-I) = WS-KEY
                 MOVE WS-I TO WW-ROW(WS-WANT-N)
             END-IF
         END-PERFORM
         IF WW-ROW(WS-WANT-N) = 0
             MOVE 2 TO WW-FOUND(WS-WANT-N)
             ADD 1 TO WS-FOUND-N
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
*>   the scan, west to east and north to south, stops when every wanted structure has a start (a name the data lacks counts as done)
     PERFORM VARYING WS-SX FROM -150 BY 1 UNTIL WS-SX > 149 OR WS-FOUND-N >= WS-WANT-N
         PERFORM VARYING WS-SZ FROM -150 BY 1 UNTIL WS-SZ > 149
             CALL "STRUCT-CHUNK-STARTS" USING CW-SEED WS-SX WS-SZ WS-COUNT
             PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-I > WS-COUNT
                 PERFORM VARYING WS-J FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-J > WS-WANT-N
                     IF SC-STRUCT(WS-I) = WW-ROW(WS-J) AND WW-ROW(WS-J) > 0 AND WW-FOUND(WS-J) = 0
                         MOVE 1 TO WW-FOUND(WS-J)
                         MOVE WS-SX TO WW-CX(WS-J)
                         MOVE WS-SZ TO WW-CZ(WS-J)
                         ADD 1 TO WS-FOUND-N
                     END-IF
                 END-PERFORM
             END-PERFORM
         END-PERFORM
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE 0 TO WS-CHUNKS
     PERFORM VARYING WS-J FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-J > WS-WANT-N
         IF WW-FOUND(WS-J) = 1
             MOVE WW-CX(WS-J) TO WS-E1
             MOVE WW-CZ(WS-J) TO WS-E2
             DISPLAY "START " FUNCTION TRIM(WW-KEY(WS-J)) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2)
             MOVE WW-KEY(WS-J) TO WS-WHAT
             COMPUTE WS-X0 = WW-CX(WS-J) - 1
             COMPUTE WS-Z0 = WW-CZ(WS-J) - 1
             MOVE 3 TO WS-N
             PERFORM DUMP-AREA
         ELSE
             DISPLAY "START " FUNCTION TRIM(WW-KEY(WS-J)) " none in 300 x 300 chunks (row " WW-ROW(WS-J) ")"
         END-IF
     END-PERFORM
*>   the 6 x 6 areas, each "x,z" the north-west chunk
     MOVE 1 TO WS-POINTER
     PERFORM UNTIL WS-POINTER > 1024
         MOVE SPACES TO WS-KEY
         UNSTRING WS-AREAS DELIMITED BY ALL SPACES INTO WS-KEY WITH POINTER WS-POINTER
         IF WS-KEY = SPACES
             EXIT PERFORM
         END-IF
         MOVE 0 TO WS-X0 WS-Z0
         MOVE SPACES TO WS-A1 WS-A2
         UNSTRING WS-KEY DELIMITED BY "," INTO WS-A1 WS-A2
         COMPUTE WS-X0 = FUNCTION NUMVAL(WS-A1)
         COMPUTE WS-Z0 = FUNCTION NUMVAL(WS-A2)
         MOVE "area" TO WS-WHAT
         MOVE WS-AREA-N TO WS-N
         PERFORM DUMP-AREA
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "test gen hashes the dump ran" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 1 TO TL-EXPECTED-N
     MOVE 1 TO TL-OBSERVED-N
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.

 DUMP-AREA.
     PERFORM VARYING WS-CX FROM WS-X0 BY 1 UNTIL WS-CX >= WS-X0 + WS-N
         PERFORM VARYING WS-CZ FROM WS-Z0 BY 1 UNTIL WS-CZ >= WS-Z0 + WS-N
             MOVE FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE TO WS-CLOCK
             PERFORM CLOCK-MS
             MOVE WS-T0 TO WS-T1
             CALL "GEN-JOB-RUN-ALL" USING WS-DIM WS-CX WS-CZ WS-REF WS-REF-Y
             MOVE FUNCTION CURRENT-DATE TO WS-CLOCK
             PERFORM CLOCK-MS
             COMPUTE WS-MS = WS-T0 - WS-T1
             MOVE 0 TO WS-CRC
             CALL "CRC32" USING WS-REF WS-CRC-LEN WS-CRC
             MOVE WS-CX TO WS-E1
             MOVE WS-CZ TO WS-E2
             MOVE WS-REF-Y TO WS-E3
             MOVE WS-CRC TO WS-E4
             MOVE WS-MS TO WS-E5
             DISPLAY "HASH " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-WHAT) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E3) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E4)
             MOVE 0 TO WS-ENT-CRC
             PERFORM VARYING WS-ENT-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-ENT-I > GE-COUNT
                 COMPUTE WS-ENT-LEN = 32 + GE-LEN(WS-ENT-I)
                 CALL "CRC32" USING GE-ENTRY(WS-ENT-I) WS-ENT-LEN WS-ENT-CRC
             END-PERFORM
             PERFORM VARYING WS-ENT-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL WS-ENT-I > GE-BOX-COUNT
                 MOVE 28 TO WS-ENT-LEN
                 CALL "CRC32" USING GE-BOX(WS-ENT-I) WS-ENT-LEN WS-ENT-CRC
             END-PERFORM
             MOVE GE-COUNT TO WS-E6
             MOVE WS-ENT-CRC TO WS-E7
             DISPLAY "ENT " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-WHAT) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E6) " " GE-BOX-COUNT " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E7)
             DISPLAY "TIME " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-WHAT) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E5)
         END-PERFORM
     END-PERFORM.

 CLOCK-MS.
     COMPUTE WS-T0 = FUNCTION NUMVAL(WS-CLOCK(9:2)) * 3600000 + FUNCTION NUMVAL(WS-CLOCK(11:2)) * 60000
         + FUNCTION NUMVAL(WS-CLOCK(13:2)) * 1000 + FUNCTION NUMVAL(WS-CLOCK(15:2)) * 10.
 END PROGRAM TEST-GEN-HASHES.

 COPY CORETEST.
